# ── build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/tanulom
/bin/
# The embedded SPA is produced by `make spa` / the Dockerfile. Only the .gitkeep
# is tracked: `//go:embed all:dist` needs the directory to contain at least one
# file, and `all:` matches dotfiles, so an empty .gitkeep is enough to make a
# fresh clone compile with `go build` and nothing else.
#
# index.html is NOT tracked. It was listed as an exception below and never
# actually committed (a bare `dist/` further down swallowed the whole directory,
# and git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded directory) — and tracking
# the real one would leave the tree permanently dirty after every SPA build.
# Anything that needs a servable placeholder writes one: `make ensure-spa`, and
# ci.yml's "Stub embedded SPA" step.
backend/internal/web/dist/*
!backend/internal/web/dist/.gitkeep
web-ui/dist/
web-ui/node_modules/
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── runtime data — never commit a learner's database ──────────
/data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ── the embedded starter pack — TRACKED ON PURPOSE ────────────
# backend/internal/lang/starter/*.gz is committed, not generated at build time,
# and no pattern here may come to cover it. //go:embed on a missing file is a
# COMPILE ERROR, so ignoring these would mean a fresh clone cannot build the
# backend at all — and a binary built without them would boot with no language
# pack, which is the exact state [ADR-010] removes. ~16 MB, refreshed by
# `make starter`, which is rare.

# ── Piper voice models — fetched, not committed ───────────────
# 60 MB each and redistributable from rhasspy/piper-voices, so they are a
# download rather than a repository. `make voices` fetches them; only the small
# .json voice cards are tracked, which is what records WHICH three voices the
# ear trainer expects and under what licence.
langpack/voices/*.onnx

# ── language pack build artefacts ─────────────────────────────
langpack/cache/
langpack/.venv/
services/mt/.venv/
langpack/build/
/dist/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ── media ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/media/
*.wav
*.opus
*.webm

# ── research PDFs that may not be redistributed ───────────────
# See .claude/research/pdf/README.md for the per-file ledger.
# These are held locally for reference but must not be published.
.claude/research/pdf/02-cepeda-2006-distributed-practice.pdf
.claude/research/pdf/02-spacing-benefit-metaanalysis.pdf

# ── editor / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ── secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config.local.yaml
# NOT a bare `dist/`. A bare pattern matches a DIRECTORY at any depth, and git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded — so it silently
# killed the `!backend/internal/web/dist/index.html` exception at the top of
# this file, the placeholder never got committed, and a fresh clone could not
# `go build` at all. `web-ui/dist/` above already covers the SPA build.
/dist/

# The tutor corpus build downloads its sources here; the outputs are committed.
langpack/cache/tutor/

.agent-context